Package: panelrate
Type: Package
Title: Robust Semiparametric Rate Regression for Panel Count Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Dayu", "Sun", email = "dayusun@iu.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits the semiparametric proportional rate model for panel count
    data, that is, for recurrent event processes observed only at intermittent
    examination times, allowing covariates to be time-varying. Estimation uses
    a nonparametric maximum likelihood approach implemented through an
    expectation-maximization algorithm under a working Poisson assumption, while
    inference does not require that assumption to hold. Two computationally
    inexpensive covariance estimators are provided: a robust sandwich estimator
    that remains consistent when the Poisson assumption fails, and an efficient
    information estimator that is a fast substitute for profile likelihood when
    it holds. The profile likelihood estimator is also available for comparison.
    Methods are described in Sun, Guo, Li, Tu and Sun (2024)
    <doi:10.3150/23-BEJ1713>.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: Rcpp, stats, graphics
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
URL: https://github.com/commintern/panelrate
BugReports: https://github.com/commintern/panelrate/issues
Config/testthat/edition: 3
NeedsCompilation: yes
